                                        "sense_id": "b9200616-10da-38a0-855e-1f9fab57aa87",
                                        "entry_id": "7e606830-46ee-3e70-a9fd-f8cd33155938",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sailor from India or Southeast Asia, especially as serving on a European ship."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "376446c6-325e-4272-b880-4c18b3b6e370",
                                                "sense_id": "b9200616-10da-38a0-855e-1f9fab57aa87",
                                                "text": "A motley crowd saunters along the streets — Lascars off a P. and O., blond Northmen from a Swedish barque, Japanese from a man-of-war, English sailors, Spaniards, pleasant-looking fellows from a French cruiser, negroes off an American tramp."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6de349fa-7a8b-48db-bdae-ef5592e61925",
                                                "sense_id": "b9200616-10da-38a0-855e-1f9fab57aa87",
                                                "text": "...and what foreigner is it, exactly, that Pirate has in mind if it isn't that stateless lascar across his own mirror-glass, that poorest of exiles..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce58206e-70e3-43d4-9a58-abe9a3791049",
                                                "sense_id": "b9200616-10da-38a0-855e-1f9fab57aa87",
                                                "text": "As for the voyage itself, his account of Mauritius, where the ship stopped, saw the appearance of Muslim lascars."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d64ab225-e383-3a03-b1a4-1a312a023131",
